[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571495331","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101117#issuecomment-2571495331","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101117","id":2571495331,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZReej","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-05T04:18:10Z","updated_at":"2025-01-05T04:18:10Z","body":"Sorry for spamming the workflow runs, I didn't see where I could run the checks locally.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571495331/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575780184","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101117#issuecomment-2575780184","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101117","id":2575780184,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zh0lY","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T16:50:09Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T16:50:09Z","body":"> I didn't see where I could run the checks locally.\r\n\r\n1. Compile with `tests=true` flag (like `scons dev_build=true tests=true`).\r\n2. Run `bin/<godot_binary> --test`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2575780184/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579177159","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101117#issuecomment-2579177159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101117","id":2579177159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zux7H","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T04:51:41Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T04:51:41Z","body":"Thanks for all the suggestions for this PR, especially documentation!\r\n\r\nI think after this is merged, [tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_exports.rst](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/blob/master/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_exports.rst) should be updated to reflect `@no_storage`, though I'm not sure where to fit this in exactly, since it is a new category of annotation. The syntax highlighting should also be updated to include this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579177159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4113346395","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101117#issuecomment-4113346395","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101117","id":4113346395,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71LK9b","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T20:01:38Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T20:01:38Z","body":"The proposal that this PR addresses had it's last activity in 2023. Since then we have added `@export_custom` which in my opinion does already solve what the proposal is asking for:\r\n\r\n> Add an annotation that can give quick access to the \"storage\" usage flag of a property.\r\n\r\nCould you elaborate why exactly you don't think `@export_custom` is a sufficient solution?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4113346395/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4113581008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101117#issuecomment-4113581008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101117","id":4113581008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71MEPQ","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-23T20:41:45Z","updated_at":"2026-03-23T20:41:45Z","body":"> Could you elaborate why exactly you don't think `@export_custom` is a sufficient solution?\r\n\r\nSome export hints are verbose and not always obvious. For example, it's not obvious that you should use `PROPERTY_USAGE_CLASS_IS_ENUM` in addition to `PROPERTY_HINT_ENUM` (if you **only** want to remove the `PROPERTY_USAGE_STORAGE` flag):\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node\r\n\r\n@export var side_1: Side\r\n@export_custom(\r\n    PROPERTY_HINT_ENUM,\r\n    \"Side Left:0,Side Top:1,Side Right:2,Side Bottom:3\",\r\n    PROPERTY_USAGE_DEFAULT | PROPERTY_USAGE_CLASS_IS_ENUM,\r\n)\r\nvar side_2: Side\r\n@export_custom(\r\n\tPROPERTY_HINT_ENUM,\r\n\t\"Side Left:0,Side Top:1,Side Right:2,Side Bottom:3\",\r\n\tPROPERTY_USAGE_EDITOR | PROPERTY_USAGE_CLASS_IS_ENUM,\r\n)\r\nvar side_3: Side\r\n#@export @no_storage var side_4: Side\r\n\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n    for property in get_property_list():\r\n        if property.usage & PROPERTY_USAGE_SCRIPT_VARIABLE:\r\n            print(property)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere are other non-obvious hints/flags (`PROPERTY_USAGE_NIL_IS_VARIANT`, `PROPERTY_HINT_ARRAY_TYPE`, `PROPERTY_HINT_DICTIONARY_TYPE`, `PROPERTY_HINT_TYPE_STRING`, `PROPERTY_HINT_RESOURCE_TYPE`, `PROPERTY_HINT_NODE_TYPE`).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4113581008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4124929598","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101117#issuecomment-4124929598","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101117","id":4124929598,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc713W4-","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-25T09:11:24Z","updated_at":"2026-03-25T09:11:24Z","body":"I get that `export_custom` isn't exactly the most user friendly API. But based on support on the proposal I don't feel like this usecase is common enough to warrant adding a new annotation.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4124929598/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4125104533","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101117#issuecomment-4125104533","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101117","id":4125104533,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc714BmV","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-25T09:40:24Z","updated_at":"2026-03-25T09:40:24Z","body":"> I don't feel like this usecase is common enough to warrant adding a new annotation\r\n\r\nThe ability to export properties without the `PROPERTY_USAGE_STORAGE` flag can be useful and desirable for tool scripts. However, the problem is that we can't introduce a single annotation (`@export_editor` or `@export_no_storage`), unlike `@export_storage`, which accomplishes the opposite (exporting a property without displaying the field in the Inspector). Because the appearance of fields can vary, we have multiple `@export_*` annotations. A modifier annotation (like `@no_storage`) is the only option with the current property export system if we want a clear and ergonomic solution.\r\n\r\nThe only existing alternative that seems acceptable to me is using `_validate_property()` to exclude `PROPERTY_USAGE_STORAGE` from specified exported properties. This is a good alternative, but it requires a bit of boilerplate and is less explicit if you have many properties in a class.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4125104533/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4183361078","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101117#issuecomment-4183361078","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101117","id":4183361078,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75WQY2","user":{"login":"zhehangd","id":9572364,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NzIzNjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9572364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd","html_url":"https://github.com/zhehangd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhehangd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-03T12:53:27Z","updated_at":"2026-04-03T13:04:47Z","body":"> > I don't feel like this usecase is common enough to warrant adding a new annotation\r\n> \r\n> The ability to export properties without the `PROPERTY_USAGE_STORAGE` flag can be useful and desirable for tool scripts. However, the problem is that we can't introduce a single annotation (`@export_editor` or `@export_no_storage`), unlike `@export_storage`, which accomplishes the opposite (exporting a property without displaying the field in the Inspector). Because the appearance of fields can vary, we have multiple `@export_*` annotations. A modifier annotation (like `@no_storage`) is the only option with the current property export system if we want a clear and ergonomic solution.\r\n> \r\n> The only existing alternative that seems acceptable to me is using `_validate_property()` to exclude `PROPERTY_USAGE_STORAGE` from specified exported properties. This is a good alternative, but it requires a bit of boilerplate and is less explicit if you have many properties in a class.\r\n\r\nOne more point: `_validate_property` does not work without `@tool`, and it seems an overkill to use it only for this purpose.\r\n\r\nGodot Engine is using no-storage/no-editor-display extensively (searching for `PROPERTY_USAGE_NONE` and `PROPERTY_USAGE_EDITOR` in the codebase gives tons of examples). We currently just cannot do it easily in GDScript. I think this fact is a sufficient reason to add it.\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4183361078/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/41